  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "REST Mental Model and Constraints",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "REST Mental Model and Constraints",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Resources",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Everything is a ==resource== (a noun) at a **URI**",
                "Clients exchange ==representations== (usually JSON) of its state"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Six Constraints",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Client-server**: UI and data split",
                "==Stateless==: each request carries all context (token, params)",
                "**Cacheable**: responses declare it",
                "**Uniform interface**: standard verbs and URIs",
                "**Layered system**: proxies, gateways",
                "**Code-on-demand**: optional"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Stateless",
              "text": "No server session between calls: any server can answer, so you ==scale horizontally==."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Methods",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Method",
                "Use",
                "Safe",
                "Idempotent"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`GET`",
                  "read",
                  "yes",
                  "yes"
                ],
                [
                  "`POST`",
                  "create",
                  "no",
                  "no"
                ],
                [
                  "`PUT`",
                  "replace",
                  "no",
                  "yes"
                ],
                [
                  "`PATCH`",
                  "partial update",
                  "no",
                  "not guaranteed"
                ],
                [
                  "`DELETE`",
                  "remove",
                  "no",
                  "yes"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Of these five, only ==GET== is safe (HEAD and OPTIONS are safe too)"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**RESTful vs just HTTP?** Resources plus all six constraints",
                "**Why stateless?** Any server serves any request, so it scales out",
                "**Safe vs idempotent?** Safe: GET. Idempotent: GET, PUT, DELETE"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Resource Naming, Nesting and Status Codes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Resource Naming, Nesting and Status Codes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Naming Rules",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Plural nouns==, lowercase **kebab-case**",
                "Never verbs: the ==HTTP method== is the verb"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Avoid",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`/getOrder?id=42`",
                  "`GET /orders/42`"
                ],
                [
                  "`/createUser`",
                  "`POST /users`"
                ],
                [
                  "`/OrderItems`",
                  "`/order-items`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Nesting",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Nest only to show ==ownership==, **1-2 levels** deep",
                "Item has a unique ID? Expose it at ==top level==: `/orders/42`",
                "Keep the nested path for ==listing==: `/users/7/orders`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Path",
                "Verdict"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`/users/7/orders`",
                  "{green:OK}, ownership"
                ],
                [
                  "`/users/7/orders/42/items/3/reviews`",
                  "{red:Too deep}"
                ],
                [
                  "`/items/3/reviews`",
                  "{green:Flattened}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Actions and Create",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Non-CRUD action: model a ==noun sub-resource==, not a verb",
                "Cancel an order: `POST /orders/42/cancellation`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "http",
              "lines": [
                "POST /orders",
                "HTTP/1.1 201 Created",
                "Location: /orders/43"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Create response",
              "text": "POST returns ==201 Created== plus a **Location** header pointing at the new resource."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Filtering, Sorting, Bodies and Error Formats",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Filtering, Sorting, Bodies and Error Formats",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Query Params on the Collection",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "http",
              "lines": [
                "GET /orders?status=paid&sort=-created_at&limit=20&cursor=abc"
              ],
              "note": "a - prefix means descending"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Filter, sort and paginate with ==query params==",
                "{green:Cursor} pagination for large or changing data",
                "{red:Offset} slows down and skips or duplicates rows as data shifts"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Bodies and Status Codes",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Send JSON with `Content-Type: application/json`",
                "==PUT== needs the full object; ==PATCH== sends only changed fields",
                "Return the created or updated resource"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Code",
                "Meaning"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "200 / 201 / 204",
                  "OK / Created / No Content"
                ],
                [
                  "400 / 422",
                  "bad input / validation failed"
                ],
                [
                  "401 / 403",
                  "unauthenticated / forbidden"
                ],
                [
                  "404 / 409",
                  "not found / conflict"
                ],
                [
                  "429 / 500",
                  "rate limited / server error"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Error Body",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "json",
              "lines": [
                "{ \"type\": \"...\",",
                "  \"title\": \"Validation failed\",",
                "  \"status\": 422,",
                "  \"detail\": \"email is invalid\",",
                "  \"errors\": [{ \"field\": \"email\" }] }"
              ],
              "note": "RFC 9457 problem+json shape"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Same shape every time",
              "text": "==401== = not logged in. ==403== = logged in but not allowed."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "HATEOAS and REST vs GraphQL vs gRPC",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "HATEOAS and REST vs GraphQL vs gRPC",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. HATEOAS",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Responses carry ==links== to the next valid actions",
                "Clients **follow links** instead of hardcoding URLs",
                "{red:Most real APIs skip it}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "json",
              "lines": [
                "{ \"id\": 42, \"status\": \"pending\",",
                "  \"_links\": {",
                "    \"pay\": \"/orders/42/payment\",",
                "    \"cancel\": \"/orders/42\" } }"
              ],
              "note": "the server decides which actions are open"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. REST vs GraphQL vs gRPC",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "REST",
                "GraphQL",
                "gRPC"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Shape",
                  "many URLs, HTTP + JSON",
                  "one endpoint, client picks fields",
                  "Protobuf over HTTP/2, strict contract"
                ],
                [
                  "Best for",
                  "public APIs",
                  "varied clients, e.g. mobile",
                  "internal service-to-service"
                ],
                [
                  "Strength",
                  "easy HTTP caching",
                  "fixes over-fetching",
                  "streaming, small payloads"
                ],
                [
                  "Risk",
                  "over- and under-fetching",
                  "harder caching; needs depth or complexity limits",
                  "browsers need gRPC-Web; hard to debug by eye"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**What does HATEOAS solve?** Hardcoded URLs: links tell clients the next valid actions",
                "**GraphQL over REST?** Varied clients that need exact fields",
                "**gRPC over REST?** Fast internal calls with a strict contract",
                "**Why is GraphQL caching harder?** One endpoint, so URL-keyed HTTP caches cannot tell queries apart"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Common REST Design Mistakes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Common REST Design Mistakes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Mistakes and Fixes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Mistake",
                "Fix"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`POST /createUser`",
                  "`POST /users`"
                ],
                [
                  "`GET /deleteOrder?id=42`",
                  "`DELETE /orders/42`"
                ],
                [
                  "`200` + error in body",
                  "`4xx` + problem+json"
                ],
                [
                  "`500` for bad input",
                  "`400` / `422`"
                ],
                [
                  "Unbounded `GET /orders`",
                  "`/v1/orders?limit=20`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "GET that changes state breaks the ==safe== contract",
                "Crawlers and prefetchers fire it: ==side effects==",
                "200 + error hides failures from clients and monitoring"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Version and Paginate Early",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Add `/v1` or a version header ==from day one==",
                "Put a ==limit== on every collection, with a max cap",
                "Unbounded lists ==break later==: slow, huge payloads"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "http",
              "lines": [
                "GET /v1/orders?limit=20&cursor=abc"
              ],
              "note": "version + limit + cursor"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Summary and Interview Points",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Status code is the contract",
              "text": "Noun URL + right method + honest status: **4xx** = client fault, **5xx** = server fault."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Version a public API?** `/v1` in path or a header; keep old versions alive",
                "**No pagination?** Huge responses, timeouts, memory pressure as data grows",
                "**Errors as 200?** Clients, caches and monitoring read only the status code"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "REST API Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "REST API Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Methods and URLs",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Method",
                "Use",
                "Idempotent"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`GET`",
                  "read",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "`POST`",
                  "create",
                  "{red:no}"
                ],
                [
                  "`PUT`",
                  "replace",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "`PATCH`",
                  "partial update",
                  "not guaranteed"
                ],
                [
                  "`DELETE`",
                  "remove",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Plural nouns, ==kebab-case==, nest at most **two levels**",
                "Filter, sort and paginate with ==query params==",
                "`-` prefix on sort means descending"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "http",
              "lines": [
                "GET /orders?status=paid&sort=-created_at&limit=20&cursor=..."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Status Codes",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Group",
                "Codes"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "{green:Success}",
                  "200 OK, ==201 + Location==, 204 No Content"
                ],
                [
                  "{orange:Client}",
                  "400 input, 401 unauthenticated, 403 forbidden, 404, 409 conflict, 422 validation, 429 rate limited"
                ],
                [
                  "{red:Server}",
                  "500"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Pick One",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:REST}: public CRUD APIs",
                "{purple:GraphQL}: flexible client-driven queries",
                "{green:gRPC}: fast internal service calls",
                "==HATEOAS== is optional"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "Design GET, POST and error responses for an /orders API",
                "Justify REST, GraphQL or gRPC for it"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Errors",
              "text": "Never return **200** with an error body. Keep ==500== for server faults only."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A user has name and email. A client sends `PUT /users/7` with only `{\"email\": \"new@x.com\"}`. What goes wrong?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "PUT replaces the whole object, so ==name is lost==",
                "Use `PATCH` to send only changed fields"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Page 1 of `/feed?offset=0&limit=20` is loaded. A new row is then inserted at the top. What does page 2 show?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "The old 20th row shifts to 21st, so it ==appears twice==",
                "Cursor pagination avoids this"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Spot the bug: `GET /orders/42/cancel` cancels an order. A link prefetcher visits it. Result?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "The order is cancelled, because GET must be ==safe==",
                "Use `POST /orders/42/cancellation`"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}